        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Prescience" hidden="true" id="3494-e945-e8bc-da7b" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="false">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="f16c-9704-f63a-b015" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="3103-61ab-0bfb-0f50" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Prescience" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait" hidden="false" id="b8ab-ec55-7fd5-1357">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">Once per game, while the Warlord is on the battlefield, the controlling player may re-roll any single dice roll (including a single dice as part of a 2D6 or multi-dice roll) made for a friendly unit with the Legiones Astartes (Grey Knights) special rule. In addition, an army whose Warlord has this Trait may make one additional Reaction during the opposing player's Movement phase, as long as the Warlord has not been removed as a casualty.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <categoryLinks>
            <categoryLink targetId="1158-146a-d9a0-39ad" id="9dad-143a-c283-d9aa" primary="true" name="Warlord Traits:" />
          </categoryLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Knight of the Flame" hidden="true" id="e7fc-094f-f782-8450" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="false">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="fcdf-96a7-d7bc-2110" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="a1a3-6142-5bed-53ca" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Knight of the Flame" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait" hidden="false" id="aeca-4ded-82ac-a343">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">A Warlord with this Trait, and any unit he joins, gains the Fearless special rule. In addition, an army whose Warlord has this Trait may make one additional Reaction during the opposing player's Assault phase, as long as the Warlord has not been removed as a casualty.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <categoryLinks>
            <categoryLink targetId="1158-146a-d9a0-39ad" id="9a35-8109-4098-9704" primary="true" name="Warlord Traits:" />
          </categoryLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0" />
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
  </sharedSelectionEntryGroups>
  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Loyalist" id="7e5b-1687-5d45-76d8" hidden="false" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
      <description>A Grey Knights army must take the Loyalist Allegiance; it may never be Traitor.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="The Aegis" id="f384-a120-63d6-aaf2" hidden="false" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
      <description>All models with the Legiones Astartes (Grey Knights) special rule gain Adamantium Will (5+) and Shrouded (6+). In addition, enemy units making Shooting Attacks against a model with the Legiones Astartes (Grey Knights) special rule treat that model as being 3" further away than it actually is when determining weapon range, the effects of Special Rules, and whether a model is within a specified distance. When making Psychic Checks, units composed entirely of models with the Legiones Astartes (Grey Knights) special rule may re-roll Psychic Check results of 1.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Legiones Astartes (Grey Knights)" id="9ade-e6da-6ebe-c8d6" hidden="false" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
      <description>All models with the Legiones Astartes (Grey Knights) special rule gain the Preferred Enemy (Daemons) and Stubborn special rules.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Brotherhood of Psykers" id="9a82-d3a3-4eaf-9404" hidden="false" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
      <description>Every Grey Knight is a psyker: a model with this special rule has the Psyker Unit Sub-type. Its psychic powers come only from its datasheet: the Brotherhood Psyker and Brotherhood Librarian special rules, a Psychic Discipline it names, and any Minor Psychic Power it selects or carries. Psychic checks are made against the unit's Leadership; a failed check causes Perils of the Warp as in the 2.0 rulebook†.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Brotherhood Psyker" id="a06c-a50b-e14c-bb0d" hidden="false" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
      <description>This model must select one Minor Psychic Power and one Psychic Discipline (Dominus, Sanctic, Anathemata, Divination or Telepathy). A model that already carries a Minor Psychic Power from its datasheet's Wargear keeps it and selects a second, so it has two; this is an exception to the Minor Psychic Powers rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Brotherhood Librarian" id="30e4-f198-63af-7fc7" hidden="false" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
      <description>This model must select one Minor Psychic Power and two Psychic Disciplines. Only one Psychic Discipline may be used per Combat Turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Core Psychic Discipline List" id="1a02-7c17-e539-b477" hidden="false" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
      <description>Any Psyker that selects a Psychic Discipline also gains the Aetheric Lightning Psychic Weapon. This includes the Dominus, Sanctic, Anathemata, Divination and Telepathy Disciplines. *Aetheric lightning is the fury of the Warp itself, coalesced and given form by the will of the psyker and directed at their foes like a storm of eldritch power.* Weapon: Range, Str, AP, Type. Aetheric Lightning: 18", 3, 4, Assault 4, Force. Force: Any Psyker with a weapon or ability with this special rule may choose to make a Psychic check before making any attacks with that weapon or resolving the ability. If the test is successful then the Strength value of any attacks made is doubled. If the test is failed then a Perils of the Warp attack is resolved targeting the unit containing the model that failed its test. If the Psyker survives Perils of the Warp then it may attack as normal.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Dreadknight Talon" id="e872-2c7c-82f7-b2f6" hidden="false" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
      <description>When deployed onto the battlefield (either at the start of the battle or when arriving from Reserves), all models with this special rule in a unit must be placed within unit coherency but afterwards operate independently and are not treated as a unit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Minor Psychic Powers" id="8dae-272b-41c6-ee22" hidden="false" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
      <description>Models with this special rule know one or more Minor Psychic Powers. All models with the Brotherhood Psyker or Brotherhood Librarian special rule must select one Minor Psychic Power from the Minor Psychic Powers below during army selection, before the beginning of the battle; a datasheet that lists a Minor Psychic Power in its Wargear gives that power to every model in the unit instead. If a unit includes more than one model that must select a Minor Psychic Power, all those models must select the same power. No model may have or use more than one Minor Psychic Power, unless another special rule specifically states that it can. Unless otherwise specified, a Minor Psychic Power may be activated once per Phase at the time indicated in its description. To activate a Minor Psychic Power, the controlling player must make a Psychic Check using the Leadership Characteristic of the Psyker activating the power. If the Psychic Check is successful, resolve the effects of the power immediately. If the Psychic Check is failed, the power has no effect. If the Psychic Check results in Perils of the Warp, resolve the effects as normal. A model or unit may only attempt to activate each Minor Psychic Power once per Phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Nemesis Force" id="c4fb-6217-c3b3-5be9" hidden="false" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
      <description>The controlling player of any unit that includes one or more models with the Psyker Unit Sub-type and a weapon or ability with this special rule may choose to activate this special rule before making any attacks with that weapon or resolving the ability. To activate this special rule, the controlling player must make a single Psychic Check using the Leadership Characteristic of any model in the unit that does not have the Independent Character Special Rule (unless the unit is entirely composed of models with the Independent Character Special Rule, in which case the controlling player may select which model's Leadership Characteristic is used). If the Check is successful, the Strength value of all attacks made with weapons or abilities with this special rule is increased by +2. In addition, all attacks made with weapons or abilities with this special rule gain Rending (6+) and Murderous Strike (6+). When targeting models with the Daemon Unit Type, attacks made with weapons or abilities with this special rule instead gain Rending (4+) and Murderous Strike (4+). If a weapon already possesses Rending and/or Murderous Strike, improve the value of each by +1 to a maximum of Rending (4+) and Murderous Strike (4+), or Rending (3+) and Murderous Strike (3+) when targeting models with the Daemon Unit Type. These benefits last until the end of the current Phase. If the Check is failed, no benefit is gained, but the models in that unit may attack as normal. This can trigger Perils of the Warp.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Teleport Strike" id="df3e-b9ef-b7f6-8dc6" hidden="false" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
      <description>Grey Knights in Aegis Terminator armour, Strike Squads and Interceptor Squads have Deep Strike, and do not scatter if any friendly Grey Knights unit is within 6" of the target point†.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Apothecarion Detachment" id="f89b-5770-4109-0fa1" hidden="false" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
      <description>A Brother Apothecary unit is selected as any other unit, using up a single Force Organisation slot and bought in the same manner. However, before the first turn begins and any models are deployed, every model in it must be assigned to another unit from the same Detachment. A Brother Apothecary may only be assigned to a unit composed entirely of Infantry models with the same Brotherhood (X) special rule as the Apothecary; to be assigned to a Brotherhood Terminator Squad or a Paladin Squad, the Apothecary must wear Aegis Terminator armour. No Brother Apothecary may be assigned to a unit that includes one or more models with the Independent Character special rule or the Unique Sub-type (but such models may join a unit that includes a Brother Apothecary as normal during deployment or any following turn). No more than one Brother Apothecary may be assigned to any given unit. Once assigned, the Apothecary is part of that unit and may not leave it under any circumstances; if that unit is removed as a casualty, the Apothecary is removed as well. In battles using Victory points, no Victory points are ever scored for removing a Brother Apothecary as a casualty. When assigned to a unit, a Brother Apothecary gains all of the special rules (except those that specifically forbid it) and Unit Sub-types listed for that unit, but does not gain access to any additional Wargear options available to it.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Techmarine Covenant" id="0eae-0080-c466-8f38" hidden="false" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
      <description>A Brotherhood Techmarine unit is selected as any other unit, using up a single Force Organisation slot and bought in the same manner. However, before the first turn begins and any models are deployed, every model in it must be assigned to another unit from the same Detachment. A Brotherhood Techmarine may only be assigned to a unit composed entirely of models with the Infantry Unit Type and the same Brotherhood (X) special rule as the Techmarine, and may not join a unit with Terminator armour of any kind. No Brotherhood Techmarine may be assigned to a unit that includes one or more models with the Independent Character special rule or the Unique Sub-type (but such models may join a unit that includes a Brotherhood Techmarine as normal during deployment or any following turn). No more than one Brotherhood Techmarine may be assigned to any given unit. Once assigned, the Techmarine is part of that unit and may not leave it under any circumstances; if that unit is removed as a casualty, the Techmarine is removed as well. In battles using Victory points, no Victory points are ever scored for removing a Brotherhood Techmarine as a casualty. When assigned to a unit, a Brotherhood Techmarine gains all of the special rules (except those that specifically forbid it) and Unit Sub-types listed for that unit, but does not gain access to any additional Wargear options available to it.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Brotherhood (X)" id="4749-6b7c-76d3-27ab" hidden="false" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
      <description>When building an army, choose one Brotherhood for each detachment. Every unit in that detachment gains Brotherhood (X). Kaldor Draigo and Castellan Crowe may join any Brotherhood; Brother-Captain Stern only the 3rd Brotherhood; Grand Master Voldus only the 3rd Brotherhood. Each Brotherhood's Advanced Reaction is available in addition to Psychic Ward and costs one point of the Reaction Allotment†.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Invulnerable Save (X)" id="2e5e-c3f1-d335-9842" hidden="false" publicationId="c336-0f01-71db-7a8f">
      <description>The model has an Invulnerable Save of X, which may be taken against any Wound instead of its armour save.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
  <catalogueLinks>
    <catalogueLink name="Legions Astartes" targetId="6393-649c-7213-a327" type="catalogue" importRootEntries="false" id="c6ca-f69e-2c0d-66ef" />
